  "summary": "Prices ending in 99 trick human brains due to the left-digit effect, where numbers are processed left to right, making $2.99 feel much closer to $2.00 than $3.00. Retailers have used this strategy for over a century, and studies show 99 endings signal deals that can even cause $39 items to outsold $34 items.",
